This project ships with vendored third-party source and depends on external
components that are each governed by their own licenses. See THIRDPARTY.md
for the full list and each dependency's terms. In particular:

  - swift/Sources/RMScene/ is a direct copy of Rick Lupton's rmscene-swift
    (MIT; see swift/Sources/RMScene/LICENSE for the preserved upstream
    copyright notice).
  - rmapi (ddvk/rmapi, AGPL-3.0) is a runtime dependency invoked as a
    separate process via subprocess. rmsync does not link to, embed, or
    redistribute rmapi source or binaries — users install it themselves
    (typically via ``brew install io41/tap/rmapi``). Per GPL/AGPL
    aggregation principles, the copyleft obligations of AGPL-3.0 apply
    only to rmapi itself, not to rmsync.
